    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "body": "### Problem\n\nWhen `vimgrep` is running in ui1/vim, about once per second a message with the currently processed file path is shown in the cmdline as a busy indication.\n\nWith ui2 enabled, there is no busy indication while it's running: the messages are queued up and only show in the end, all at once. Furthermore, the path list in the end is typically a small subset of processed files, but can easily be interpreted as a list of matching files.\n\n`ui_call_event(\"msg_show\", args);` is called in time, but the corresponding lua code is deferred.\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n```\nnvim --clean +\"lua require('vim._core.ui2').enable()\"\n:vimgrep PATTERN **\n```\n\n### Expected behavior\n\nThere should be a live progress/busy indicator.\nIdeally ui-messges of kind \"progress\".\n(Personally, I would prefer the number of files that have been processed so far.)\n\n### Nvim version (nvim -v)\n\nv0.13.0-dev-990+g73bb6a8a5e\n\n### Vim (not Nvim) behaves the same?\n\nno, vim 9.2\n\n### Operating system/version\n\nNixOS 26.05\n\n### Terminal name/version\n\nalacritty 0.17.0\n\n### $TERM environment variable\n\nalacritty\n\n### Installation\n\nbuild from repo",
    "closed_at": null,
    "closed_by": null,
