            "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
            "body": "No, it didn't fix it. I could only find 1 commit, but I also tried reverting #29446.\n\nIt's not a recent regression, the same problem is in nvim 0.12, otherwise I would have bisected (sorry, should have mentioned..).\n\nThe UI is not \"busy\" while vimgrep tries to write the message. Here's a typical sequence:\n```\nui_busy_start: busy = 1\nui_busy_stop: busy = 0\nvgr_display_name\nvgr_display_name\nvgr_display_name\n...\nui_busy_start: busy = 1\nui_busy_stop: busy = 0\n```\nAnd nothing changes when I surround `vgr_display_name` with `ui_busy_start()...ui_busy_stop()`. It seems unrelated.",
